  "verdict": "In the forced-coherence regime (r_global >= 0.7 - the regime Model B is actually about, since below it nothing is being forced) the tree carries 1.22x the lattice's dissonance at matched coherence - in the predicted direction, but small. The claim is regime-specific, not general: below r_global = 0.7 the same ratio is 0.86, and the *peak* dissonance the three geometries can reach is near-identical (0.99x tree over lattice), so the version of the prediction stated in IX.7 - much higher dissonance on the tree than the lattice at the same drive - does not hold. Only the refined version does. On the defect claim the two readouts disagree, which is informative: local incoherence is 1.21x higher at branch points than a degree-matched null predicts, but IX.5's own statistic - the phase step from a parent segment to the mean of its daughters - is 0.86x the same step along ordinary chain segments, i.e. no larger at branch points at all. Branch points show more neighbourhood disagreement simply because they have more neighbours; the phase discontinuity Model B predicts them to carry is not there.",
  "figures": [
